---
import BaseLayout from "@/components/BaseLayout.astro";
import PageHeader from "@/components/ui/PageHeader.astro";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Terms of Service"
  description="Terms of Service for Prayer Wall"
  breadcrumbs={[{ name: "Home", href: "/" }, { name: "Terms of Service" }]}
>
  <script
    slot="head"
    type="application/ld+json"
    set:html={JSON.stringify({
      "@context": "https://schema.org",
      "@type": "WebPage",
      name: "Terms of Service - Prayer Wall",
      description: "Terms of Service for Prayer Wall.",
      url: "https://prayerwall.space/terms",
      isPartOf: {
        "@type": "WebSite",
        name: "Prayer Wall",
        url: "https://prayerwall.space",
      },
    })}
  />
  <div class="space-y-6 max-w-3xl">
    <PageHeader
      eyebrow="Legal"
      title="Terms of Service"
      description="By using Prayer Wall, you agree to these terms. Please read them carefully."
    />

    <article class="prose prose-sm max-w-none text-(--color-text-muted)">
      <section>
        <h2 class="heading-serif text-xl font-semibold text-(--color-text)">1. Acceptance of Terms</h2>
        <p class="mt-2">
          By accessing or using Prayer Wall ("the Service"), you agree to be bound by these Terms of Service ("Terms").
          If you do not agree to these Terms, you may not use the Service.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="mt-8">
        <h2 class="heading-serif text-xl font-semibold text-(--color-text)">2. Description of Service</h2>
        <p class="mt-2">
          Prayer Wall is a platform for sharing prayer requests and praying for others. The Service allows users to
          submit prayer requests publicly or privately, and for community members to pray for those requests.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="mt-8">
        <h2 class="heading-serif text-xl font-semibold text-(--color-text)">3. User Accounts</h2>
        <p class="mt-2">
          You may use the Service as a registered user or anonymously. Registered accounts require a valid email address
          and email verification. Anonymous access is provided via a token-based identity that expires after a period of
          inactivity.
        </p>
        <p class="mt-2">
          You are responsible for maintaining the confidentiality of your account credentials and management tokens. You
          agree to accept responsibility for all activities that occur under your account or token.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="mt-8">
        <h2 class="heading-serif text-xl font-semibold text-(--color-text)">4. Content Guidelines</h2>
        <p class="mt-2">When submitting prayer requests, you agree not to post content that:</p>
        <ul class="mt-2 list-disc list-inside space-y-1">
          <li>Is illegal, harmful, threatening, abusive, harassing, defamatory, or hateful</li>
          <li>Infringes on intellectual property rights</li>
          <li>Contains private personal information of others without consent</li>
          <li>Is spam, commercial solicitation, or off-topic content</li>
          <li>Promotes violence, self-harm, or illegal activities</li>
        </ul>
        <p class="mt-2">We reserve the right to remove any content that violates these guidelines.</p>
      </section>

      <section class="mt-8">
        <h2 class="heading-serif text-xl font-semibold text-(--color-text)">5. Privacy</h2>
        <p class="mt-2">
          Your privacy is important to us. Please review our <a href="/privacy" class="underline hover:opacity-80"
            >Privacy Policy</a
          > to understand how we collect, use, and protect your information.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="mt-8">
        <h2 class="heading-serif text-xl font-semibold text-(--color-text)">6. Intellectual Property</h2>
        <p class="mt-2">
          The Service and its original content, features, and functionality are owned by Prayer Wall and are protected
          by international copyright, trademark, and other intellectual property laws. You retain ownership of the
          prayer requests you submit.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="mt-8">
        <h2 class="heading-serif text-xl font-semibold text-(--color-text)">7. Disclaimers</h2>
        <p class="mt-2">
          The Service is provided "as is" and "as available" without warranties of any kind, either express or implied.
          We do not guarantee that the Service will be uninterrupted, secure, or error-free.
        </p>
        <p class="mt-2">
          Prayer Wall is a community platform and not a substitute for professional counseling, medical advice, or
          emergency services. If you are in crisis, please contact emergency services or a crisis helpline immediately.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="mt-8">
        <h2 class="heading-serif text-xl font-semibold text-(--color-text)">8. Limitation of Liability</h2>
        <p class="mt-2">
          To the maximum extent permitted by law, Prayer Wall shall not be liable for any indirect, incidental, special,
          consequential, or punitive damages, including loss of profits, data, or use, arising from your use of the
          Service.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="mt-8">
        <h2 class="heading-serif text-xl font-semibold text-(--color-text)">9. Termination</h2>
        <p class="mt-2">
          We may terminate or suspend your access to the Service at any time, with or without cause, including for
          violation of these Terms. Upon termination, your right to use the Service will immediately cease.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="mt-8">
        <h2 class="heading-serif text-xl font-semibold text-(--color-text)">10. Changes to Terms</h2>
        <p class="mt-2">
          We may modify these Terms at any time. We will notify users of material changes by posting the new Terms on
          this page. Your continued use of the Service after changes constitutes acceptance of the new Terms.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="mt-8">
        <h2 class="heading-serif text-xl font-semibold text-(--color-text)">11. Governing Law</h2>
        <p class="mt-2">
          These Terms shall be governed by and construed in accordance with the laws of the jurisdiction in which Prayer
          Wall operates, without regard to its conflict of law provisions.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="mt-8">
        <h2 class="heading-serif text-xl font-semibold text-(--color-text)">12. Contact</h2>
        <p class="mt-2">
          If you have questions about these Terms, please contact us through the platform or visit our <a
            href="/donate"
            class="underline hover:opacity-80">Support</a
          > page.
        </p>
      </section>

      <p class="mt-10 text-sm text-(--color-text-muted)">
        Last updated: {new Date().toLocaleDateString("en-US", { year: "numeric", month: "long", day: "numeric" })}
      </p>
    </article>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
